-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1, PART 2: FORMATION OF THE CONTRACT (ss 2 to 15A).
-- Reading a result (NOTES.md, "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING"): JUST TRUE and JUST FALSE are
-- answers the text gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer on these facts".
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- Section 11(5), 12(6), 13(4), 14(6) and 15(3) point to the Schedule: those gates are in soga-schedule.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`

§ `Part 2 -- Formation of the contract`

§§ `Contract of sale (ss 2 and 3)`

-- s 2(1).  "Contract of sale of goods" and "the price" are defined by their own words.
-- src:214 | 2.—(1) A contract of sale of goods is a contract by which the seller
-- src:215 | transfers or agrees to transfer the property in goods to the buyer for a
-- src:216 | money consideration, called the price.
@ref s 2(1) (src:214-216)
GIVEN `the seller transfers or agrees to transfer the property in goods to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is for a money consideration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(1) the contract is a contract of sale of goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller transfers or agrees to transfer the property in goods to the buyer` AND `it is for a money consideration`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A contract of sale of goods is a contract by which the seller transfers or agrees to transfer the property in goods to the buyer for a money consideration, called the price."
            -- MARGINAL (a): "is a contract by which" is read as a definition, like "means", so a contract lacking either limb is not a contract of sale of goods; the other reading is that the sentence only describes the usual case and is silent about the rest.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 2(1) "the price": the money consideration is called the price.
-- src:215 | transfers or agrees to transfer the property in goods to the buyer for a
-- src:216 | money consideration, called the price.
@ref s 2(1) the price (src:215-216)
GIVEN `the money consideration for the transfer of the property in the goods` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `s 2(1) the price` IS
    `the money consideration for the transfer of the property in the goods`

-- s 2(2).  "There may be a contract of sale between one part owner and another."
-- src:218 | (2) There may be a contract of sale between one part owner and
-- src:219 | another.
@ref s 2(2) (src:218-219)
GIVEN `the seller is a part owner of the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer is another part owner of the same goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(2) there may be a contract of sale between one part owner and another` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller is a part owner of the goods` AND `the buyer is another part owner of the same goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection says only that a contract of sale may exist between one part owner and another; it does not say that no other contract of sale may exist.
            NOTHING

-- s 2(3).  "A contract of sale may be absolute or conditional."  The Act does not define "conditional",
-- so whether the contract is conditional is a fact the person states.
-- src:221 | (3) A contract of sale may be absolute or conditional.
@ref s 2(3) (src:221)
GIVEN `the contract of sale is subject to a condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Absolute or conditional`
DECIDE `s 2(3) the contract of sale is absolute or conditional` IS
    IF `the contract of sale is subject to a condition`
    THEN `a conditional contract`
    ELSE `an absolute contract`

-- s 2(4).  A sale: the property is transferred from seller to buyer under the contract.
-- src:223 | (4) Where under a contract of sale the property in the goods is
-- src:224 | transferred from the seller to the buyer, the contract is called a sale.
@ref s 2(4) (src:223-224)
GIVEN `under the contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Stage of the contract`
DECIDE `s 2(4) the contract is called a sale` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `under the contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer`
        THEN JUST `a sale`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the contract "a sale" only "Where under a contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer"; s 2(5) names the other case. The yes/no twin `s 2(4) the rule naming the contract a sale applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 2(4) the contract is called a sale`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:223 | (4) Where under a contract of sale the property in the goods is
-- src:224 | transferred from the seller to the buyer, the contract is called a sale.
@ref s 2(4) applies (src:223-224)
GIVEN `under the contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(4) the rule naming the contract a sale applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `under the contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where under a contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer, the contract is called a sale." -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 2(5).  An agreement to sell: the transfer is at a future time or on a condition still to be fulfilled.
-- src:226 | (5) Where under a contract of sale the transfer of the property in the
-- src:227 | goods is to take place at a future time or subject to some condition
-- src:228 | later to be fulfilled, the contract is called an agreement to sell.
@ref s 2(5) (src:226-228)
GIVEN `the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is subject to some condition later to be fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Stage of the contract`
DECIDE `s 2(5) the contract is called an agreement to sell` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time` OR `the transfer is subject to some condition later to be fulfilled`
        THEN JUST `an agreement to sell`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection names the contract "an agreement to sell" only "Where under a contract of sale the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time or subject to some condition later to be fulfilled". The yes/no twin `s 2(5) the rule naming the contract an agreement to sell applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 2(5) the contract is called an agreement to sell`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:226 | (5) Where under a contract of sale the transfer of the property in the
-- src:227 | goods is to take place at a future time or subject to some condition
-- src:228 | later to be fulfilled, the contract is called an agreement to sell.
@ref s 2(5) applies (src:226-228)
GIVEN `the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is subject to some condition later to be fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(5) the rule naming the contract an agreement to sell applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time` OR `the transfer is subject to some condition later to be fulfilled`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where under a contract of sale the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time or subject to some condition later to be fulfilled, the contract is called an agreement to sell." -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 2(6).  An agreement to sell becomes a sale when the time elapses or the conditions are fulfilled.
-- src:230 | (6) An agreement to sell becomes a sale when the time elapses or
-- src:231 | the conditions are fulfilled subject to which the property in the goods
-- src:232 | is to be transferred.
@ref s 2(6) (src:230-232)
GIVEN `the time has elapsed subject to which the property is to be transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions have been fulfilled subject to which the property is to be transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 2(6) the agreement to sell becomes a sale` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the time has elapsed subject to which the property is to be transferred` OR `the conditions have been fulfilled subject to which the property is to be transferred`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection says an agreement to sell "becomes a sale when the time elapses or the conditions are fulfilled"; until then it has not become a sale under this subsection ("when" read as "where": fork F10). -- ruled 2026-11-05 (w): "when" read as "where" (ruled 2026-11-05: "when" counts as "where"; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- E1 option B, gathered by hand (NOTES.md, fork register): ss 2(4), (5) and (6) each name the contract; this
-- function gathers the three answers so a reader sees the stage of the contract in one place.  Each section's
-- own function above gives its own answer (option C); this one only combines them.
-- src:223 | (4) Where under a contract of sale the property in the goods is
-- src:224 | transferred from the seller to the buyer, the contract is called a sale.
-- src:226 | (5) Where under a contract of sale the transfer of the property in the
-- src:227 | goods is to take place at a future time or subject to some condition
-- src:228 | later to be fulfilled, the contract is called an agreement to sell.
-- src:230 | (6) An agreement to sell becomes a sale when the time elapses or
-- src:231 | the conditions are fulfilled subject to which the property in the goods
-- src:232 | is to be transferred.
@ref ss 2(4), (5), (6) (src:223-232)
GIVEN `under the contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is subject to some condition later to be fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time has elapsed subject to which the property is to be transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions have been fulfilled subject to which the property is to be transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Stage of the contract`
DECIDE `ss 2(4) to (6) the stage of the contract of sale` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 2(4) the contract is called a sale` `under the contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer` EQUALS JUST `a sale`
        THEN JUST `a sale`
        IF `s 2(6) the agreement to sell becomes a sale` `the time has elapsed subject to which the property is to be transferred` `the conditions have been fulfilled subject to which the property is to be transferred` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST `a sale`
        IF `s 2(5) the contract is called an agreement to sell` `the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time` `the transfer is subject to some condition later to be fulfilled` EQUALS JUST `an agreement to sell`
        THEN JUST `an agreement to sell`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): none of s 2(4), (5) or (6) is met on these facts. The yes/no twin `ss 2(4) to (6) a rule naming the stage of the contract applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `ss 2(4) to (6) the stage of the contract of sale`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- function gathers the three answers so a reader sees the stage of the contract in one place.  Each section's
-- own function above gives its own answer (option C); this one only combines them.
-- src:223 | (4) Where under a contract of sale the property in the goods is
-- src:224 | transferred from the seller to the buyer, the contract is called a sale.
-- src:226 | (5) Where under a contract of sale the transfer of the property in the
-- src:227 | goods is to take place at a future time or subject to some condition
-- src:228 | later to be fulfilled, the contract is called an agreement to sell.
-- src:230 | (6) An agreement to sell becomes a sale when the time elapses or
-- src:231 | the conditions are fulfilled subject to which the property in the goods
-- src:232 | is to be transferred.
@ref ss 2(4), (5), (6) applies (src:223-232)
GIVEN `under the contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transfer is subject to some condition later to be fulfilled` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time has elapsed subject to which the property is to be transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions have been fulfilled subject to which the property is to be transferred` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 2(4) to (6) a rule naming the stage of the contract applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `under the contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred from the seller to the buyer` OR `the transfer of the property in the goods is to take place at a future time` OR `the transfer is subject to some condition later to be fulfilled` OR `the time has elapsed subject to which the property is to be transferred` OR `the conditions have been fulfilled subject to which the property is to be transferred`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where under a contract of sale the property in the goods is transferred ... Where ... the transfer ... is to take place at a future time or subject to some condition ... An agreement to sell becomes a sale when the time elapses or the conditions are fulfilled" -- none of the three -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 3(1).  Capacity is governed by the general law, which is outside the sources: the person says what it gives.
-- src:236 | 3.—(1) Capacity to buy and sell is regulated by the general law
-- src:237 | concerning capacity to contract and to transfer and acquire property.
@ref s 3(1) (src:236-237)
GIVEN `the general law concerning capacity to contract and to transfer and acquire property gives the party capacity` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(1) the party has capacity to buy and sell` IS
    CONSIDER `the general law concerning capacity to contract and to transfer and acquire property gives the party capacity`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer
    -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Capacity to buy and sell is regulated by the general law concerning capacity to contract and to transfer and acquire property", which is not among the sources.
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

-- s 3(2) and (3).  Necessaries sold and delivered to a minor or a person incompetent to contract.
-- src:243 | (3) In subsection (2), “necessaries” means goods suitable to the
-- src:244 | condition in life of the minor or other person concerned and to his
-- src:245 | actual requirements at the time of the sale and delivery.
@ref s 3(3) (src:243-245)
GIVEN `the goods are suitable to the condition in life of the minor or other person concerned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are suitable to his actual requirements at the time of the sale and delivery` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(3) the goods are necessaries` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods are suitable to the condition in life of the minor or other person concerned` AND `the goods are suitable to his actual requirements at the time of the sale and delivery`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“necessaries” means goods suitable to the condition in life of the minor or other person concerned and to his actual requirements at the time of the sale and delivery"
            JUST FALSE

-- src:239 | (2) Where necessaries are sold and delivered to a minor or to a
-- src:240 | person who by reason of mental incapacity or drunkenness is
-- src:241 | incompetent to contract, he must pay a reasonable price for them.
@ref s 3(2) (src:239-241)
GIVEN `the goods are necessaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods were sold and delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer is a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer is incompetent to contract by reason of mental incapacity or drunkenness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable price for the goods` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 3(2) the amount the buyer must pay for necessaries sold and delivered` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the goods are necessaries`
         AND `the goods were sold and delivered`
         AND (`the buyer is a minor` OR `the buyer is incompetent to contract by reason of mental incapacity or drunkenness`)
        THEN JUST `a reasonable price for the goods`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises "Where necessaries are sold and delivered to a minor or to a person who by reason of mental incapacity or drunkenness is incompetent to contract"; other cases are for the general law (s 3(1)). The yes/no twin `s 3(2) the duty to pay a reasonable price for necessaries applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 3(2) the amount the buyer must pay for necessaries sold and delivered`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:239 | (2) Where necessaries are sold and delivered to a minor or to a
-- src:240 | person who by reason of mental incapacity or drunkenness is
-- src:241 | incompetent to contract, he must pay a reasonable price for them.
@ref s 3(2) applies (src:239-241)
GIVEN `the goods are necessaries` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods were sold and delivered` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer is a minor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer is incompetent to contract by reason of mental incapacity or drunkenness` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 3(2) the duty to pay a reasonable price for necessaries applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods are necessaries` AND `the goods were sold and delivered` AND (`the buyer is a minor` OR `the buyer is incompetent to contract by reason of mental incapacity or drunkenness`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where necessaries are sold and delivered to a minor or to a person who by reason of mental incapacity or drunkenness is incompetent to contract, he must pay a reasonable price for them." -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Formalities of contract (s 4)`

-- s 4(1).  "Subject to this and any other Act": whether another enactment requires a form is outside the sources.
-- src:254 | 4.—(1) Subject to this and any other Act, a contract of sale may be
-- src:255 | made in writing (either with or without seal), or by word of mouth, or
-- src:256 | partly in writing and partly by word of mouth, or may be implied from
-- src:257 | the conduct of the parties.
@ref s 4(1) (src:254-257)
GIVEN `the form of the contract` IS A `Form of the contract of sale`
      `another enactment requires a particular form or formality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(1) a contract of sale may be made in this form` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `another enactment requires a particular form or formality`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to this and any other Act" -- another Act is not among the sources.
            NOTHING
        IF `the form of the contract` EQUALS `made in some other form`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the subsection names writing (with or without seal), word of mouth, partly in writing and partly by word of mouth, and implied from conduct; it does not say that no other form is allowed.
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 4(2).  "Nothing in this section affects the law relating to corporations."
-- src:259 | (2) Nothing in this section affects the law relating to corporations.
@ref s 4(2) (src:259)
GIVEN `the question is the law relating to corporations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 4(2) section 4 affects the law relating to corporations` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the question is the law relating to corporations`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section affects the law relating to corporations."
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of the law relating to corporations.
            NOTHING

§§ `Subject matter of contract (ss 5 to 7)`

-- s 5(1).  Existing goods, or future goods ("goods to be manufactured or acquired by him after the making of the contract").
-- src:265 | 5.—(1) The goods which form the subject of a contract of sale may
-- src:266 | be existing goods, owned or possessed by the seller, or goods to be
-- src:267 | manufactured or acquired by him after the making of the contract of
-- src:268 | sale, in this Act called future goods.
@ref s 5(1) (src:265-268)
GIVEN `the goods are existing goods owned or possessed by the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are to be manufactured or acquired by the seller after the making of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1) the goods may be the subject of a contract of sale` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods are existing goods owned or possessed by the seller` OR `the goods are to be manufactured or acquired by the seller after the making of the contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be existing goods ... or goods to be manufactured or acquired" does not say that goods of no such kind cannot be the subject of a contract of sale.
            NOTHING

-- src:266 | be existing goods, owned or possessed by the seller, or goods to be
-- src:267 | manufactured or acquired by him after the making of the contract of
-- src:268 | sale, in this Act called future goods.
@ref s 5(1) future goods (src:266-268)
GIVEN `the goods are to be manufactured or acquired by the seller after the making of the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(1) the goods are future goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the goods are to be manufactured or acquired by the seller after the making of the contract`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "goods to be manufactured or acquired by him after the making of the contract of sale, in this Act called future goods" (and s 61(1): "“future goods” means goods to be manufactured or acquired by the seller after the making of the contract of sale").
            JUST FALSE

-- s 5(2).
-- src:270 | (2) There may be a contract for the sale of goods the acquisition of
-- src:271 | which by the seller depends on a contingency which may or may not
-- src:272 | happen.
@ref s 5(2) (src:270-272)
GIVEN `the seller's acquisition of the goods depends on a contingency which may or may not happen` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(2) there may be a contract for the sale of goods whose acquisition depends on a contingency` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller's acquisition of the goods depends on a contingency which may or may not happen`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks only of goods whose acquisition by the seller depends on a contingency.
            NOTHING

-- s 5(3).  A present sale of future goods operates as an agreement to sell.
-- src:274 | (3) Where by a contract of sale the seller purports to effect a present
-- src:275 | sale of future goods, the contract operates as an agreement to sell the
-- src:276 | goods.
@ref s 5(3) (src:274-276)
GIVEN `the seller purports to effect a present sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are future goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Stage of the contract`
DECIDE `s 5(3) a purported present sale of future goods operates as an agreement to sell` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller purports to effect a present sale` AND `the goods are future goods`
        THEN JUST `an agreement to sell`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "Where by a contract of sale the seller purports to effect a present sale of future goods". The yes/no twin `s 5(3) the rule that a purported present sale of future goods operates as an agreement to sell applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 5(3) a purported present sale of future goods operates as an agreement to sell`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:274 | (3) Where by a contract of sale the seller purports to effect a present
-- src:275 | sale of future goods, the contract operates as an agreement to sell the
-- src:276 | goods.
@ref s 5(3) applies (src:274-276)
GIVEN `the seller purports to effect a present sale` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods are future goods` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 5(3) the rule that a purported present sale of future goods operates as an agreement to sell applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller purports to effect a present sale` AND `the goods are future goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where by a contract of sale the seller purports to effect a present sale of future goods, the contract operates as an agreement to sell the goods." -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 6.  Specific goods that had perished, without the seller's knowledge, when the contract was made.
-- src:280 | 6. Where there is a contract for the sale of specific goods, and the
-- src:281 | goods without the knowledge of the seller have perished at the time
-- src:282 | when the contract is made, the contract is void.
@ref s 6 (src:280-282)
GIVEN `the contract is for the sale of specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods had perished when the contract was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller did not know that the goods had perished` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 6 the contract is void` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the contract is for the sale of specific goods`
         AND `the goods had perished when the contract was made`
         AND `the seller did not know that the goods had perished`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "Where there is a contract for the sale of specific goods, and the goods without the knowledge of the seller have perished at the time when the contract is made"; where the seller knew, or the goods had not perished, the section does not apply. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 7.  An agreement to sell specific goods, which perish without fault before the risk passes.
-- src:286 | 7. Where there is an agreement to sell specific goods and
-- src:287 | subsequently the goods, without any fault on the part of the seller
-- src:288 | or buyer, perish before the risk passes to the buyer, the agreement is
-- src:289 | avoided.
@ref s 7 (src:286-289)
GIVEN `there is an agreement to sell specific goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods perished after the agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there was no fault on the part of the seller or the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods perished before the risk passed to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7 the agreement to sell is avoided` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `there is an agreement to sell specific goods`
         AND `the goods perished after the agreement`
         AND `there was no fault on the part of the seller or the buyer`
         AND `the goods perished before the risk passed to the buyer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "Where there is an agreement to sell specific goods and subsequently the goods, without any fault on the part of the seller or buyer, perish before the risk passes to the buyer". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

§§ `Price (ss 8 and 9)`

-- s 8(1).  The price may be fixed by the contract, left to be fixed in an agreed manner, or determined by course of dealing.
-- src:298 | 8.—(1) The price in a contract of sale may be fixed by the contract,
-- src:299 | or may be left to be fixed in a manner agreed by the contract, or may
-- src:300 | be determined by the course of dealing between the parties.
@ref s 8(1) (src:298-300)
GIVEN `the price is fixed by the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price is left to be fixed in a manner agreed by the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price is determined by the course of dealing between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(1) the price is determined as the subsection mentions` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the price is fixed by the contract`
          OR `the price is left to be fixed in a manner agreed by the contract`
          OR `the price is determined by the course of dealing between the parties`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be fixed by the contract, or ... agreed ..., or ... determined by the course of dealing" -- s 8(2) speaks of a price "not determined as mentioned in subsection (1)" and is the provision that answers that case.
            NOTHING

-- s 8(2).  If none of the three ways of s 8(1) fixes the price, the buyer must pay a reasonable price.
-- src:302 | (2) Where the price is not determined as mentioned in
-- src:303 | subsection (1), the buyer must pay a reasonable price.
@ref s 8(2) (src:302-303)
GIVEN `the price is fixed by the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price is left to be fixed in a manner agreed by the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price is determined by the course of dealing between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable price on the circumstances of the case` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 8(2) the amount the buyer must pay where the price is not determined` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   (NOT `the price is fixed by the contract`)
         AND (NOT `the price is left to be fixed in a manner agreed by the contract`)
         AND (NOT `the price is determined by the course of dealing between the parties`)
        THEN JUST `a reasonable price on the circumstances of the case`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty arises "Where the price is not determined as mentioned in subsection (1)"; where it is determined, s 8(1) leaves the price to that determination. The yes/no twin `s 8(2) the duty to pay a reasonable price applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 8(2) the amount the buyer must pay where the price is not determined`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:302 | (2) Where the price is not determined as mentioned in
-- src:303 | subsection (1), the buyer must pay a reasonable price.
@ref s 8(2) applies (src:302-303)
GIVEN `the price is fixed by the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price is left to be fixed in a manner agreed by the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price is determined by the course of dealing between the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(2) the duty to pay a reasonable price applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the price is fixed by the contract`) AND (NOT `the price is left to be fixed in a manner agreed by the contract`) AND (NOT `the price is determined by the course of dealing between the parties`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the price is not determined as mentioned in subsection (1), the buyer must pay a reasonable price." -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 8(3).  What a reasonable price is, is a question of fact; the Act supplies no figure.
-- src:305 | (3) What is a reasonable price is a question of fact dependent on the
-- src:306 | circumstances of each particular case.
@ref s 8(3) (src:305-306)
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 8(3) the Act's own figure for a reasonable price` IS
    -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): "What is a reasonable price is a question of fact dependent on the circumstances of each particular case"; the Act gives no number, so the amount is a fact the person states (the input `a reasonable price on the circumstances of the case` of s 8(2)).
    NOTHING

-- s 9(1), first limb.  Valuation by a third party fails: the agreement is avoided.
-- src:310 | 9.—(1) Where there is an agreement to sell goods on the terms that
-- src:311 | the price is to be fixed by the valuation of a third party, and he cannot
-- src:312 | or does not make the valuation, the agreement is avoided; but if the
-- src:313 | goods or any part of them have been delivered to and appropriated by
-- src:314 | the buyer, he must pay a reasonable price for them.
