      `the third party cannot make the valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the third party does not make the valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(1) the agreement to sell is avoided` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the agreement to sell is on terms that the price is to be fixed by the valuation of a third party`
         AND (`the third party cannot make the valuation` OR `the third party does not make the valuation`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the subsection applies "Where there is an agreement to sell goods on the terms that the price is to be fixed by the valuation of a third party, and he cannot or does not make the valuation". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 9(1), proviso.  "But if the goods or any part of them have been delivered to and appropriated by the buyer, he must pay a reasonable price for them."
-- src:310 | 9.—(1) Where there is an agreement to sell goods on the terms that
-- src:311 | the price is to be fixed by the valuation of a third party, and he cannot
-- src:312 | or does not make the valuation, the agreement is avoided; but if the
-- src:313 | goods or any part of them have been delivered to and appropriated by
-- src:314 | the buyer, he must pay a reasonable price for them.
