      `the goods or some part of them have been delivered to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods or some part of them have been appropriated by the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable price for the goods delivered and appropriated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `s 9(1) the amount the buyer must pay for goods delivered to and appropriated by him` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the valuation by the third party failed`
         AND `the goods or some part of them have been delivered to the buyer`
         AND `the goods or some part of them have been appropriated by the buyer`
        THEN JUST `a reasonable price for the goods delivered and appropriated`
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "but if the goods or any part of them have been delivered to and appropriated by the buyer, he must pay a reasonable price for them" -- the duty is stated only for that case. The yes/no twin `s 9(1) the duty to pay a reasonable price for goods delivered and appropriated applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 9(1) the amount the buyer must pay for goods delivered to and appropriated by him`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:310 | 9.—(1) Where there is an agreement to sell goods on the terms that
-- src:311 | the price is to be fixed by the valuation of a third party, and he cannot
-- src:312 | or does not make the valuation, the agreement is avoided; but if the
-- src:313 | goods or any part of them have been delivered to and appropriated by
-- src:314 | the buyer, he must pay a reasonable price for them.
@ref s 9(1) proviso applies (src:310-314)
GIVEN `the valuation by the third party failed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods or some part of them have been delivered to the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods or some part of them have been appropriated by the buyer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(1) the duty to pay a reasonable price for goods delivered and appropriated applies` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the valuation by the third party failed` AND `the goods or some part of them have been delivered to the buyer` AND `the goods or some part of them have been appropriated by the buyer`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
