            JUST FALSE

-- s 9(2).  Who may sue when the third party is prevented from valuing by the fault of the seller or the buyer.
-- src:316 | (2) Where the third party is prevented from making the valuation by
-- src:317 | the fault of the seller or buyer, the party not at fault may maintain an
-- src:318 | action for damages against the party at fault.
@ref s 9(2) (src:316-318)
GIVEN `the third party is prevented from making the valuation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the seller is at fault` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer is at fault` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Party to the sale`
DECIDE `s 9(2) the party who may maintain an action for damages against the party at fault` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the third party is prevented from making the valuation` AND `the seller is at fault` AND (NOT `the buyer is at fault`)
        THEN JUST Buyer
        IF `the third party is prevented from making the valuation` AND `the buyer is at fault` AND (NOT `the seller is at fault`)
        THEN JUST Seller
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection gives the action to "the party not at fault" where the third party is prevented "by the fault of the seller or buyer"; where both are at fault, or neither, it is silent. The yes/no twin `s 9(2) the action for damages against the party at fault applies` answers JUST FALSE here (ruled 2026-11-05 (b)); a function that returns a value cannot say no.
            NOTHING

-- Twin of `s 9(2) the party who may maintain an action for damages against the party at fault`: yes or no, does the rule apply? (ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if")
-- src:316 | (2) Where the third party is prevented from making the valuation by
