        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This subsection applies to a contract of sale in the case of which there appears from the contract or is to be inferred from its circumstances an intention that the seller should transfer only such title as he or a third person may have."
            -- MARGINAL (a): the sentence defines the class of contracts to which the subsection applies, so a contract outside that class is outside it; the other reading is that a "case of which" clause is a "where" clause and a contract outside it leaves the subsection silent.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 12(1).  Implied condition that the seller has (or will have) a right to sell.
