-- s 12(5).  In a limited-title contract, implied warranty that none of three kinds of person will disturb quiet possession.
-- src:401 | (5) In a contract to which subsection (3) applies, there is also an
-- src:402 | implied warranty that none of the following will disturb the buyer’s
-- src:403 | quiet possession of the goods, namely:
-- src:405 | (a) the seller;
-- src:407 | (b) in a case where the parties to the contract intend that the
-- src:408 | seller should transfer only such title as a third person may
-- src:409 | have, that person;
-- src:411 | (c) anyone claiming through or under the seller or that third
-- src:412 | person otherwise than under a charge or encumbrance
-- src:413 | disclosed or known to the buyer before the contract is
-- src:414 | made.
@ref s 12(5) (src:401-414)
GIVEN `subsection (3) applies to the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer's quiet possession is disturbed by the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the parties intend that the seller should transfer only such title as a third person may have` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer's quiet possession is disturbed by that third person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer's quiet possession is disturbed by anyone claiming through or under the seller or that third person` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person claims under a charge or encumbrance disclosed or known to the buyer before the contract was made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 12(5) the implied warranty that none of the named persons will disturb quiet possession is broken` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `subsection (3) applies to the contract`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the warranty is given "In a contract to which subsection (3) applies".
            NOTHING
        IF `the buyer's quiet possession is disturbed by the seller`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the parties intend that the seller should transfer only such title as a third person may have` AND `the buyer's quiet possession is disturbed by that third person`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the buyer's quiet possession is disturbed by anyone claiming through or under the seller or that third person` AND (NOT `that person claims under a charge or encumbrance disclosed or known to the buyer before the contract was made`)
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the buyer's quiet possession is disturbed by anyone claiming through or under the seller or that third person` AND `that person claims under a charge or encumbrance disclosed or known to the buyer before the contract was made`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the warranty covers disturbance by those claiming through or under the seller or the third person "otherwise than under a charge or encumbrance disclosed or known to the buyer" -- the list is closed by "namely" -- ruled 2026-11-05 (m): marginal rule (a) applied where it had been left out: a warranty or condition whose content is met, or whose subject the text takes out in its own words, is the text's no
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): the warranty names the seller, the third person and those claiming through or under either "otherwise than under a charge or encumbrance disclosed or known to the buyer"; it does not speak of any other disturbance.
            NOTHING

