            NOTHING
        IF `section 14(2), (3) or (4) provides an implied condition or warranty on these facts` OR `section 15 provides an implied condition on these facts`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Except as provided by this section and section 15" -- the provision that provides it gives the answer (s 14(2) to (5), s 15).
            NOTHING
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there is no implied condition or warranty about the quality or fitness for any particular purpose of goods supplied under a contract of sale"
