      `it is an appropriate case for this aspect` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(2B) the aspect is an aspect of the quality of the goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the aspect` EQUALS `the state and condition of the goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the aspect` EQUALS `some other aspect`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "the quality of goods includes their state and condition and the following (among others)" -- the list is not closed.
            NOTHING
        IF `it is an appropriate case for this aspect`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the listed aspects are aspects of quality "in appropriate cases".
