-- s 14(2C).  What the condition of satisfactory quality does not extend to.
-- src:470 | (2C) The condition implied by subsection (2) does not extend to
-- src:471 | any matter making the quality of goods unsatisfactory —
-- src:473 | (a) which is specifically drawn to the buyer’s attention before
-- src:474 | the contract is made;
-- src:476 | (b) where the buyer examines the goods before the contract is
-- src:477 | made, which that examination ought to reveal; or
-- src:479 | (c) in the case of a contract for sale by sample, which would
-- src:480 | have been apparent on a reasonable examination of the
-- src:481 | sample.
@ref s 14(2C) (src:470-481)
GIVEN `the matter was specifically drawn to the buyer's attention before the contract was made` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer examined the goods before the contract was made and that examination ought to have revealed the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a sale by sample and the matter would have been apparent on a reasonable examination of the sample` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(2C) the condition implied by s 14(2) extends to the matter making the quality unsatisfactory` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   `the matter was specifically drawn to the buyer's attention before the contract was made`
          OR `the buyer examined the goods before the contract was made and that examination ought to have revealed the matter`
          OR `it is a sale by sample and the matter would have been apparent on a reasonable examination of the sample`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The condition implied by subsection (2) does not extend to any matter making the quality of goods unsatisfactory"
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- fork F9 (decided 2026-11-05, assumed, not ruled): s 14(2) is the general rule and (2C) takes out three matters, so for any other matter the condition does extend; the rejected reading is that (2C) only subtracts and says nothing about the rest (NOTHING).
            JUST TRUE

-- s 14(3).  Particular purpose made known: implied condition of reasonable fitness, unless the buyer does not rely.
