      `the buyer expressly or by implication makes a particular purpose known to the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the price is payable by instalments and the goods were previously sold by a credit-broker to the seller` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer expressly or by implication makes a particular purpose known to the credit-broker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances show that the buyer does not rely on the skill or judgment of the seller or credit-broker` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the circumstances show that it is unreasonable for the buyer to rely on the skill or judgment of the seller or credit-broker` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(3) there is an implied condition that the goods are reasonably fit for the purpose made known` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the seller sells the goods in the course of a business`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the condition is implied "Where the seller sells goods in the course of a business". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF NOT (   `the buyer expressly or by implication makes a particular purpose known to the seller`
                OR (`the price is payable by instalments and the goods were previously sold by a credit-broker to the seller` AND `the buyer expressly or by implication makes a particular purpose known to the credit-broker`))
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the condition is implied where the buyer makes known "any particular purpose" to the seller or (in the instalment case) the credit-broker. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the circumstances show that the buyer does not rely on the skill or judgment of the seller or credit-broker` OR `the circumstances show that it is unreasonable for the buyer to rely on the skill or judgment of the seller or credit-broker`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where the circumstances show that the buyer does not rely, or that it is unreasonable for him to rely, on the skill or judgment of the seller or credit-broker"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "except where" is read as the text's no when the buyer does not rely or it is unreasonable to rely.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

