      `the other is not selling in the course of a business` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer knows that fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `reasonable steps are taken to bring that fact to the notice of the buyer before the contract is made` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 14(5) the sale by the agent is treated as a sale by a principal in the course of a business` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the person selling is acting as agent for another in the course of a business`
        THEN
            -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection applies "to a sale by a person who in the course of a business is acting as agent for another".
            NOTHING
        IF `the other is not selling in the course of a business` AND (`the buyer knows that fact` OR `reasonable steps are taken to bring that fact to the notice of the buyer before the contract is made`)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "except where that other is not selling in the course of a business and either the buyer knows that fact or reasonable steps are taken to bring it to the notice of the buyer before the contract is made"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "except where" is read as the text's no for that case.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 15(1).  Sale by sample.
-- src:520 | 15.—(1) A contract of sale is a contract for sale by sample where
-- src:522 | there is an express or implied term to that effect in the contract.
@ref s 15(1) (src:520-522)
GIVEN `there is an express or implied term that the sale is by sample` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(1) the contract of sale is a contract for sale by sample` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `there is an express or implied term that the sale is by sample`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): a contract is a contract for sale by sample "where there is an express or implied term to that effect"; a contract without such a term is not one for sale by sample under this subsection. -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 15(2).
-- src:524 | (2) In the case of a contract for sale by sample, there is an implied
-- src:525 | condition —
-- src:527 | (a) that the bulk will correspond with the sample in quality;
-- src:532 | (b) that the goods will be free from any defect, making their
-- src:533 | quality unsatisfactory, which would not be apparent on
-- src:534 | reasonable examination of the sample.
@ref s 15(2) (src:524-534)
GIVEN `the contract is for sale by sample` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(2) there are implied conditions as to correspondence with the sample and freedom from defects` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the contract is for sale by sample`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the conditions are implied "In the case of a contract for sale by sample". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (k): "in the case of" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE

-- src:524 | (2) In the case of a contract for sale by sample, there is an implied
-- src:525 | condition —
-- src:527 | (a) that the bulk will correspond with the sample in quality;
@ref s 15(2)(a) (src:524-527)
GIVEN `the contract is for sale by sample` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the bulk corresponds with the sample in quality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(2)(a) the implied condition that the bulk will correspond with the sample in quality is broken` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the contract is for sale by sample`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the condition is implied "In the case of a contract for sale by sample". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (k): "in the case of" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the bulk corresponds with the sample in quality`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there is an implied condition (a) that the bulk will correspond with the sample in quality" -- on these facts it does.
            -- MARGINAL (a): a condition whose content is met is read as the text's no to its breach.
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:524 | (2) In the case of a contract for sale by sample, there is an implied
-- src:525 | condition —
-- src:532 | (b) that the goods will be free from any defect, making their
-- src:533 | quality unsatisfactory, which would not be apparent on
-- src:534 | reasonable examination of the sample.
@ref s 15(2)(b) (src:524-525) (src:532-534)
GIVEN `the contract is for sale by sample` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the goods have a defect making their quality unsatisfactory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the defect would not be apparent on reasonable examination of the sample` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15(2)(b) the implied condition that the goods will be free from a defect not apparent on examination of the sample is broken` IS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the contract is for sale by sample`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the condition is implied "In the case of a contract for sale by sample". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (k): "in the case of" read as "where" (assumed, not ruled; fork F10): the condition not met is the text's no
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the goods have a defect making their quality unsatisfactory` AND `the defect would not be apparent on reasonable examination of the sample`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the goods have a defect making their quality unsatisfactory`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the condition covers only a defect "which would not be apparent on reasonable examination of the sample". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (m): marginal rule (a) applied where it had been left out: a warranty or condition whose content is met, or whose subject the text takes out in its own words, is the text's no
            JUST FALSE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "there is an implied condition (b) that the goods will be free from any defect, making their quality unsatisfactory" -- on these facts they are.
            -- MARGINAL (a): a condition whose content is met is read as the text's no to its breach.
            JUST FALSE

-- s 15A(1) and (2).  A slight breach in a non-consumer case is treated only as a breach of warranty.
-- src:544 | 15A.—(1) Where in the case of a contract of sale —
-- src:546 | (a) the buyer would, apart from this subsection, have the right
-- src:547 | to reject goods by reason of a breach on the part of the
-- src:548 | seller of a condition implied by section 13, 14 or 15; but
-- src:550 | (b) the breach is so slight that it would be unreasonable for the
-- src:551 | buyer to reject them,
-- src:553 | then, if the buyer does not deal as consumer, the breach is not to be
-- src:554 | treated as a breach of condition but may be treated as a breach of
-- src:555 | warranty.
-- src:557 | (2) This section applies unless a contrary intention appears in, or is
-- src:558 | to be implied from, the contract.
@ref s 15A(1), (2) (src:544-558)
GIVEN `the buyer would, apart from this subsection, have the right to reject the goods by reason of the seller's breach of a condition implied by section 13, 14 or 15` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the breach is so slight that it would be unreasonable for the buyer to reject the goods` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the buyer deals as consumer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a contrary intention appears in, or is to be implied from, the contract` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15A(1) the breach is not treated as a breach of condition but may be treated as a breach of warranty` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `a contrary intention appears in, or is to be implied from, the contract`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "This section applies unless a contrary intention appears in, or is to be implied from, the contract."
            -- MARGINAL (a): "unless" is read as the text's no when a contrary intention appears.
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the buyer deals as consumer`
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "then, if the buyer does not deal as consumer, the breach is not to be treated as a breach of condition"
            -- MARGINAL (a): "if the buyer does not deal as consumer" is read as a condition whose failure is the text's no.
            JUST FALSE
        IF `the buyer would, apart from this subsection, have the right to reject the goods by reason of the seller's breach of a condition implied by section 13, 14 or 15` AND `the breach is so slight that it would be unreasonable for the buyer to reject the goods`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): the section applies "Where ... the buyer would, apart from this subsection, have the right to reject goods ...; but the breach is so slight that it would be unreasonable for the buyer to reject them". -- ruled 2026-11-05 (b): a "where" condition not met is the text's no, like "if"
            JUST FALSE

-- s 15A(3).  The burden is on the seller.
-- src:560 | (3) It is for the seller to show that a breach fell within
-- src:561 | subsection (1)(b).
@ref s 15A(3) (src:560-561)
GIVEN `the seller has shown that the breach fell within subsection (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 15A(3) the breach is treated as one that fell within subsection (1)(b)` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `the seller has shown that the breach fell within subsection (1)(b)`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "It is for the seller to show that a breach fell within subsection (1)(b)."
            -- MARGINAL (a): a burden rule is read as the text's no when the seller has not shown it; the other reading is that the text says only who must show, and is silent on the outcome of not showing.
            JUST FALSE
